.h2 Starting and leaving [appterm-leave]
.ix Child programs, terminal
.ix Preview, terminal
The terminal is taken at the start and given back at the end.  In the course of
a session it is given back for a short time in these cases.
.table 23 37
When | What happens to the terminal
Edit / Preview / Print | The Document Manager gives the terminal to the
  | Editor, which
 Document in the Document Manager | takes it and gives it back when it ends.
Preview | The terminal is given back to the shell while
  | the Viewer shows the pages in its own window,
  | and taken again when the Viewer is closed.
  | Without an X display the Preview is refused.
.end
Nothing of this needs a key from you except the {k:Q} that closes the Viewer.

